{
  "schema": "lantern-works-site-stats/1",
  "generated_at": "2026-11-28T07:40:51Z",
  "note": "Weekly (ISO week, UTC) aggregate counts only. No IP addresses, user agents, cookies, keys or per-caller data. ref is the ?ref= channel tag. Refs ci, qa, test, smoke, house-*, readonly-* and t<N>/t<N>-* are our own checks and are excluded from external_mcp_tool_calls. Calls with no ref are counted separately in untagged_mcp_tool_calls and may include our own checks. feed_fetches_by_ref counts only feed fetches through the hosted worker, not GitHub Pages feed hits. mcp_initialize_by_ref['mcp-registry'] is probably MCP Registry health checks, not users.",
  "sources": {
    "feed_fetches": "hosted worker only (lantern-works-mcp.lantern-works.workers.dev/api/...); GitHub Pages feed hits are not counted",
    "mcp_initialize_mcp_registry": "probably MCP Registry health checks, not users",
    "hosted_mcp": "https://lantern-works-mcp.lantern-works.workers.dev/stats",
    "telemetry": "opt-in LANTERN_TELEMETRY=1 aggregate",
    "outbound_clicks": "T135 agreed click count: server-side /go/<deal-id> redirects (telemetry worker D1, aggregate day x deal x provider x src x ref x ua_class; no IPs, user agents or cookies), minus known bots, crawlers, link previews, HTTP scripts and prefetches (ua_class bot|script|prefetch) and minus our own test traffic (src *-test or internal ref). Per week in clicks {count, by_provider, by_source, excluded, unclassified_ua}.",
    "beacon_out_events": "Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon /e/out/ virtual page views (site JavaScript only), weekly total; a cross-check, not the click count",
    "clicks_reconciliation": "T135: before Nov 11 2026, outbound_clicks was the Web Analytics beacon's /e/out/ count, which only fires from site JavaScript, while go_clicks counted every server-side /go/ redirect (mostly src=feed). The week of Nov 2 (2026-W45) had 19 /go/ redirects (all src=feed, no ref, 17 providers, Nov 6-7 UTC) and 0 beacon events, so the two never measured the same thing. outbound_clicks now equals clicks.count; the beacon figure is kept as beacon_out_events. Clicks recorded before the UA filter shipped have no UA class and are counted but reported in clicks.unclassified_ua, not dropped or relabelled.",
    "page_views": "Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon page views (site b392c8b3...), real pages only, weekly total",
    "visits_by_ref": "Cloudflare Web Analytics /e/ref/<ref>/ virtual views, sent once per landing with ?ref= by pages built from 2026-11-02 (rel055) on; earlier weeks cannot show refs",
    "installs_by_ref": "opt-in LANTERN_TELEMETRY=1 collector /v1/stats installs aggregates (no raw install ids). distinct_installs = unique install ids seen that ISO week. returning_installs = install ids seen that week that were also observed on two or more distinct UTC days in the 120-day stats window (the other day may fall outside the week). installs_by_ref = distinct ids per ref that week. version 0.0.0 is excluded. Telemetry is off by default.",
    "receipts_funnel": "T55: Receipts (MCP test summaries) measured apart from GPU demand. page_views = beacon views of /receipts/ pages; visits_by_ref / mcp_initialize_by_ref / mcp_tool_calls_by_ref = refs matching receipts or receipts-<channel> only. json_fetches and link_visits are counted server-side by the hosted worker (see sources.receipts_hosted); direct GitHub Pages fetches publish no counts. Independent inquiries arrive by email and are not published here (null).",
    "go_clicks": "telemetry worker /go/<deal-id>?src= redirect (aggregate day x deal x provider x src x ref x ua_class in D1; no IPs, user agents or cookies). go_clicks_by_provider = clicks.count split by provider and src. test_go_clicks_by_provider = our own test clicks (src *-test or internal ref)",
    "agent_query_to_click": "T136: agent_query_to_click = agent_mcp_clicks / agent_tool_calls per ISO week. agent_tool_calls = hosted worker tool calls (hits kind=tool) minus house traffic (src_class house, or a house ref: ci, qa, test, smoke, house-*, readonly-*, t<N>) and known bots. agent_mcp_clicks = clicks.by_source.mcp (the src=mcp /go/ links in MCP results), already without bots and house clicks. Clicks also come from local (stdio) installs, whose calls the hosted worker cannot see, so the rate can overstate hosted-only conversion. null when no agent calls.",
    "receipts_hosted": "T137: json_fetches counts api/v1/receipts.json and receipts-proof-pack.json fetched through the hosted worker (https://lantern-works-mcp.lantern-works.workers.dev/api/v1/receipts.json?ref=receipts-<channel>); direct GitHub Pages fetches publish no counts and are not included. link_visits counts tagged Receipts links through the hosted worker's /receipts/ redirect (302 to the same page on the site). Both exclude house traffic (src_class house or a house ref) and known bots, and are split by ref.",
    "demand_daily": "P8: daily aggregate demand from hosted GPU tool calls (compare_gpu_prices, estimate_job_cost, optimize_agent_stack): one count per UTC day x tool x gpu_family x region_group x price_tier x cheapest_provider. gpu_family is the requested GPU bucketed to a fixed list of known families (anything else 'other', none 'any'); region_group is the requested region bucketed likewise; price_tier and cheapest_provider describe the first-ranked result in our answer ('none' when there was none). No caller IDs, raw arguments or free text are stored. House traffic and known bots are not counted. Hosted endpoint only; local (stdio) installs are not included."
  },
